window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Last night, I saw a murderer kill someone in cold blood. Today, I'm expected to sell my business to some hotshot billionaire. The problem? They're the same person.</b></p> <p>Arsen Isakov is the rich A-hole trying to buy out my family's dance studio after my father's death. I wanted to give him a piece of my mind and tell him that we'd never sell. But the moment he sat down across the table from me, I realized I'd seen him before.</p> <p>Last night, in fact. When he killed a man in cold blood.</p> <p>He says he's prepared to discuss the sale with me over drinks. The place he picks? The same place where I saw him kill someone.</p> <p>I know what he's capable of. I know better than to refuse his demand. So, against my better judgment, I agree.</p> <p>When I arrive, he tells me that he's the only one who can keep me and my mother safe from someone even worse than him. In exchange, I must play my role, walk down the aisle, and pretend to be his bride.</p> <p>Simple, right?</p> <p>But that was before our very fake wedding started having very real consequences. Before I learn the dark terrible truths. About Arsen. About my family.</p> <p>And about a shared past between us that I never knew.</p> <p>Sinful Devotion<i> is book one of the Grachev Bratva duet. Galina and Arsen's story continues in book two, </i>Sinful Obsession. <i>This is not a standalone. For mature listeners.</i></p>"; 
